From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hexagonrpcd: map ODM inputs and allow explicit scratch registry IO

Piano sensorspd reads /odm/etc/sensors/config/json.lst and opens its registry/DIR
marker for writing. Retain the upstream read-only default. With explicit -w,
serve actual file creation/truncation/append/update/write/remove on a private
registry copy. Other mappings remain read-only. Refuse symlink, hardlink and
non-regular writable targets; return real byte counts/errors, never stub success.

Protocol references: Qualcomm fastrpc v1.0.7 apps_std.h/apps_std_imp.c and Luca
Weiss's linux-msm/hexagonrpc PR #21, head 9f987970f9bc3e72081b7966a1f4e766ce6af6f7
(methods 5 and 24). No fake-write/remove or unverified fd-method stubs are imported.
Existing HexagonFS and apps_std code/structure remain the implementation.
Reviewed liuqin 7df47f82's registry sibling/property patches, but do not import
board-specific inputs or property semantics not requested by piano.

The new test invokes the actual apps_std handlers and maps stock data byte for
byte; it also checks write confinement and read-only defaults. Close dependent
virtual descriptors before their root, and reject descriptor aliases for empty
/root paths. Remove the patch when upstream supports the same ODM mapping and
explicit writable registry contract and these tests pass there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
